# PORT
# PENDING-SAME-HEAD; PENDING-GRAMMAR(batch-four); no blessed snapshots.
# Original tests/effects.rs `callbacks_entry_effects_are_only_io`; predicates
# migrated. Rust asserted `EffectBudget::summary_line_for_program`, which
# unions the direct rows reached through call edges and ignores the
# unknown-callee flag. The stored callback call `w.step(4)` is such an unknown
# callee (Rust helpers_call_values.rs records it maximal, as sema does here),
# so the solved `inferred_effects` of `run` is the maximal set. The same walk
# is asserted on the rows: `run` names only IO directly, and its one callee
# edge reaches no effect.
step: jet check {root}/Examples/Basics/Functions/Callbacks.jet
exit: 0
step: jet inspect rights {root}/Examples/Basics/Functions/Callbacks.jet --json
exit: 0
json: stdout doc $.callables[?name="run"] #= 1
json: stdout doc $.callables[?name="run"][0].effects.direct = ["IO"]
json: stdout doc $.callables[?name="run"][0].effects.callees = ["Callbacks::apply_twice"]
json: stdout doc $.callables[?name="apply_twice"][0].inferred_effects = []
